# Test: Tab in a session of the running ze offers an external plugin's commands and argument leaf
#
# Question: when an external plugin brings a -cmd module, does Tab in a session
# of the running ze offer the plugin's commands under their container
# (`show acme-monitor ` offers status and target) and the argument leaf the
# command node declares (`show acme-monitor target ` offers name)?
# Why not a unit test: TestEditorCompletesExternalRootFromThePublishedSet
# proves the completer reads the published set for config. Only a session on a
# real daemon proves the operational tree the session factory builds
# (buildCommandTree, cmd/ze/hub/session_factory.go) holds the commands and the
# leaf of a module a live plugin declared at boot.
#
# What the screen shows, read from the producing code: the menu after Tab on
# `show acme-monitor ` names both children (TreeCompleter.matchChildren). A
# string leaf is offered by its name, and a lone candidate is applied to the
# line by Tab (Model.handleTab), as for a compiled-in command with a mandatory
# string leaf, so `name` is on the screen either way; the typed text holds
# neither `status` nor `name`. The leaf's type enumerates no value, so no value
# is offered.
#
# VALIDATES: spec-plugin-external-yang-at-startup AC-31.
# PREVENTS: an external plugin's commands that answer when typed whole and are
#   never offered by completion.
#
# Method: the compiled fixture
# (internal/test/fixture/ui_fixture_external_yang_command_help.go) starts a
# daemon with the external-yang plugin in its `commands` variant, waits until
# the plugin answers its command, and drives a plain ssh client under a
# pseudo-terminal on the operational prompt.
#
# The timeout is DECLARED because this file starts a daemon and drives two
# interactive terminal sessions, each with a settling window.
option=timeout:value=90s

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=le test fixture ui/external-yang-command-completion $PORT
expect=exit:code=0
expect=stdout:contains=OK: Tab offered status and target, and the argument leaf name of target
reject=stdout:pattern=ZE-OBSERVER-FAIL
